# Flat Within-Mouse Triplet 5 FPS Evaluation

This notebook records the held-out benchmark for the triplet model whose dense
spatial edges are restricted to keypoints belonging to the same mouse. It also
compares that model with the fully connected dense-triplet model to isolate the
effect of removing cross-mouse edges.

## Evaluation contract

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Source FPS | 30 |
| Frame step | 6 |
| Effective FPS | 5 |
| Observation | 16 frames / 3.2 seconds |
| Prediction | 24 frames / 4.8 seconds |
| Test windows | 1,000 |
| Seed | 42 |
| Window digest | `cc1ec3dc18ded599943a7963bf082063c6bb260589626ce9dc26a1377f9fc8b0` |
| Checkpoint | `checkpoints/flat_within_mouse_triplet_5fps/flat_best.pt` |
| Checkpoint epoch | 50 |
| Validation loss | -6.540739 |

The dense and within-mouse triplet benchmarks have the same window digest,
motion thresholds, and low/medium/high counts. Their results are therefore a
paired comparison over the same held-out examples.

